"Gorgon is a nonhuman who works the lobby desk of the Artonan consulate in Chicago."
"He is one of the only nonhumans in Chicago; no other member of his species is known on Earth."
"He is about five feet tall, with smooth gray skin like a stingray's and black shark-like eyes."
"He has a wide flat nose with four nostril slits and possibly no ears."
"A couple dozen horns curve around his skull and flare into a spiky choker around his neck."
"He has long gray fingers, claws, a thick black forked tongue and translucent dark-veined eyelids."
"His voice is high-pitched, with an undertone like breaking glass."
"His laugh is a repetitive hissing."
"People call him a demon or the Desk Demon, said to come from a dimension steeped in chaos."
"The name Gorgon is likely a concession to human vocal cords."
"Glowing golden magical bindings chain him to the desk, and his wrists are raw beneath them."
"Rumor says he has been bound in the lobby forty years for trying to disembowel an Artonan."
"Online his crime is listed as attempted murder, with a life sentence."
"He can reach all public areas of the consulate but has no room of his own."
"He is barred from telling humans anything not widely known about Artonans, the System or magic."
"He cannot ask for food; it must be offered before he can accept or refuse it."
"He eats only what is freely offered: he refuses meat, dairy and eggs, yet drank offered blood."
"He watches the security monitors, avoids eye contact and needs little sleep."
"He does janitorial work and pays special attention to the windows."
"He can smell attraction and pity on humans."
"He is photographed a lot, and plushies of him are sold in at least one gift shop."
"He has dealt with two attempted bombings and a handful of enraged superhumans."
"He is the approved witness for pre-affixation class trades in his region."
"He registers new Avowed, files their paperwork and gives each a free ballpoint pen."
"His System IDs are Honorable Guest #231, name unknown, and Prisoner #12005794, called Gorgon."
"He refused the System's offer of a Contract of Service."
"His supervisor is a female Artonan, recently penalized for consorting with a demon."
"He finds scheming a cure for boredom and human adolescence beautiful and stupid."
"He owes no loyalty to human presidents or kings."
"He has asked for a confetti cannon, but it is never in the budget."
"He turns off the lobby WiFi to clear out tourists and spoils their demon photos with calm faces."
"Meeting his eyes floods a person with profound memories and knocks them out for hours."
"Alden senses him as something close to sacred and benevolent; asked if he is a god, he said no."
"He told Alden Thorn they are not friends, but that he is fond of him and wishes him well."
"He drank a few drops of Alden's freely offered blood mixed into salsa."
"From the blood he gave Alden a seventy percent chance of being chosen within six to eight months."
"He is the last of his people, whose home lies dead beyond the gates of space and time."
"He refuses the blessing of the Devouring that his predecessors accepted."
"He calls his present work revenge, like purging an infection or correcting an imbalance."
"He hinted Alden toward Rabbit by carrying his bag, saying Let me take your luggage."
"Pushing his bindings to give that hint charred his skin and left him walking stiffly in pain."
"He chewed his claws while Alden lay unconscious after affixing."
"The System says he slightly modified Alden, leaving a stabilizing presence in him."
"He lent Alden Conference Room B in the consulate basement for his first summons."
"He likes crickets."
"From Earth he sensed Alden drink Kibby's blood on Moon Thegund, and was surprised."
